## DRAFTER DECISIONS (D-n; Tuesday accepts or changes at the stamp; defaults apply if silent)
- **D-1 ONE write class: `az group delete -n hpsm-poc-demo-rg --yes --no-wait`, nothing else.** No resource-level delete, no `--force-deletion-types`, no purge, no recover, no lock removal, no role or setting write, no SQL statement, no firewall rule. Every other `az` call is a read (list/show/get).
- **D-2 `--no-wait`, then poll.** Why: the blocking form holds one CLI process open for the slowest member (SQL server, Log Analytics, the OpenAI account); if that process dies the outcome is unclear to you, while the ARM delete continues either way. The truth is read from ARM, not from the exit code: after the command returns (rc 0 only means "accepted"), poll `az group show -n hpsm-poc-demo-rg --query properties.provisioningState -o tsv` every 30 s behind an identity pass until it answers ResourceGroupNotFound, with `az group exists` as the control. Ceiling 40 minutes after the delete START; still `Deleting` then = STOP with the state and the activity-log rows (never retry, never delete a member).
- **D-3 Snapshot = settings only, never values.** App settings: NAME + sha256 of the value truncated to 12 hex + slot flag, by program (the value never printed, written or put on argv); a setting whose value is a Key Vault reference records "reference: yes" and the SECRET NAME only. Vault: properties + secret NAMES only (`az keyvault secret list`, names; a denied data-plane read = STOP, D-7). No secret, key, token, connection string or hostname in any file (hosts stay in scratch; D-9).
- **D-4 No database content.** The snapshot holds the server and database PROPERTIES (sku, state, autoPause delay, free-offer flag, max size, backup redundancy) and the firewall rules; no SQL, no `sqlcmd`, no export, no firewall rule opened. See D-5.
- **D-5 The database's content is NOT kept (Q-1, default).** The owner's card said a snapshot of SETTINGS. The deleted server takes its databases and their point-in-time backups with it: after the delete nothing of the demo data can be restored. The demo data is synthetic by design, but the demo's feedback route was ON (RELAYED, `B1286_STATUS.md:61`), so testers may have left feedback items in it: Tuesday decides at the stamp (slot S6) whether to HOLD; default is to proceed as the card said.
- **D-6 Order: nothing is deleted until every guard has passed in the SAME run, and the guard reads are repeated within 60 seconds before the delete** (identity pass, lock list, D53 end line, pane list, group resource-id list equal to the snapshot's, UAT list equal to its snapshot).
- **D-7 An authorization error anywhere = STOP.** Wrong subscription, tenant, name or user domain at the identity pass; a 403 on any read; a denied vault-secret-name list; a lock; a policy deny on the delete: the boundary working. Report it, never `az account set`, never another login, never ask for broader rights. A snapshot item that cannot be read is recorded as "not captured: <why>" and ends `STOPPED:` before the delete (an irreversible step on an incomplete snapshot is the thing to avoid).
- **D-8 Soft-deleted things are LEFT.** After the delete, READ (never act): `az keyvault list-deleted` (the vault name, `scheduledPurgeDate`, `deletionDate`), `az cognitiveservices account list-deleted`, `az monitor log-analytics workspace list-deleted-workspaces` (UNMEASURED which exist; platform soft-delete behaviour of the last two is from memory, UNMEASURED: record what the reads show). `az keyvault purge`, `recover` and the equivalents are forbidden words for the whole run.
- **D-9 Evidence is clean.** `Briefs/2026-11-05_B1303_evidence/`: no host strings (`azurewebsites.net`, `scm.`, `vault.azure.net`, `database.windows.net`: 0 each, control 1 in a scratch file), no 64-character base64 key shape beyond sha256 digests, gitleaks with a `ghp_`-shaped canary (rc 1, run WITHOUT `-r /dev/null`) and the real scan rc 0. Nothing is committed or pushed.
- **D-10 UAT is read, never written, and requested ONCE before and ONCE after:** `curl -sS -m 15 --noproxy '*' -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}'` GET of the UAT web `/` only (no other path, no cookie, never a feedback page). The only other UAT contact is read-only `az` (D-11).
- **D-11 Read scope of `az`:** `hpsm-poc-demo-rg` (everything below), `hpsm-poc-uat-rg` (list + show of its resources, for the dependency proof and the before/after list), `hpsm-poc-rg` (the dev group: list + show, scanned for the demo's tokens only), and subscription-level reads (`group list` names only; role assignments; budgets; alert rules; action groups; diagnostic settings; locks; deleted-vault/account/workspace lists). `hpsm-poc-sm-rg`, `NetworkWatcherRG` and `mpscalc-showcase-rg`: names in `az resource list` only, never `show`. Reuse the verb allow-list idea of `.tools/b1286/kit/azr.sh` (read by `sed -n`; sha256 `c2ebad8d...`, MEASURED) but WRITE YOUR OWN wrapper under a new name `azr1303.sh` (its target guard must allow exactly the three groups above and refuse the rest; no `copy and sed`), plus ONE separate script `delete1303.sh` that contains the single delete line and refuses to run unless every D-6 guard file says PASS. Copy `identity_pass.sh` from `.tools/b1286/kit/` by name, `cmp`, sha256 must equal `a3dd8d433e04a2be596f00c70a5e846fd5f8fbd36cc70f8d381ab5dc232b1afb` (MEASURED 13:16).
- **D-12 "UAT depends on nothing in the demo group" is a PROPERTY, then the checks (at least these; any other shape: prove it meets the property or STOP).** Property: no UAT resource, setting, identity, role assignment, diagnostic setting or alert names, trusts or sends to any resource inside `hpsm-poc-demo-rg`. Checks, by program, printing counts and booleans only: (a) token set T = the demo's resource names, full resource ids, `defaultHostName`s, the two user-assigned identities' client ids and principal ids, the demo vault name, the demo Application Insights instrumentation key and connection-string id, the Log Analytics workspace id and customer id, the storage account name, the OpenAI account name, the SQL server name; (b) for EVERY resource of `hpsm-poc-uat-rg` (and of `hpsm-poc-rg`) the full `show` JSON and, for each site, `az webapp config appsettings list` and `connection-string list`, scanned in-process for each token of T: expected 0 hits (**control 1: the same scan over the DEMO's own settings must hit > 0; control 2: a scratch copy of a UAT JSON with one demo token planted must hit 1; a zero without its control is no zero**); (c) every Key Vault reference in the UAT settings names a vault that is a resource of `hpsm-poc-uat-rg` (by program) and none the demo's; the UAT web and API sites' `serverFarmId`, user-assigned identity ids and SQL server in their connection strings belong to `hpsm-poc-uat-rg`; (d) `az role assignment list --all` filtered by program: assignments with scope under the demo group whose principal is a UAT identity: expected 0; assignments held by the demo identities on UAT resources: expected 0 (a non-zero is listed and is a STOP unless it is harmless AND Tuesday said so); (e) diagnostic settings of UAT resources and of the subscription: any workspace, storage or event hub target inside the demo group: expected 0; alert rules, action groups and budgets whose scope or action targets the demo group are LISTED (they go with the group or become orphans); (f) UAT group resource list (name, type, id, location, provisioningState, sorted, sha256) and the UAT sites' `state`/`defaultHostName`/`serverFarmId` before and after; (g) the Entra objects shared with UAT are named in STATUS and left alone. Any hit, any non-empty STOP list, any control that fails = `STOPPED:` before the delete.
- **D-13 Cost statement is a table, not a number.** What stops billing when the group is gone, what keeps no charge but is retained, and what is UNMEASURED (no cost API write; the drafter measured no spend). From the template (MEASURED) and the records (RELAYED): B1 plan (fixed hourly), serverless database (free offer BILLED past the allowance, `demo.bicepparam:17-18`), Log Analytics ingestion and retention, Application Insights, storage, the OpenAI deployment (pay per use), the vault (cents). Say what you could not price.

