**Step 2 - THE SNAPSHOT** into `1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-05_B1303_evidence/` (each file written once, each `az` call behind an identity pass, the commands logged without output): (1) group properties + tags and the resource list (name, type, id, location, tags, kind, sku, provisioningState); (2) both sites: `az webapp show` properties minus secrets, plan/sku, identity ids, app-settings NAMES with 12-hex value hashes (D-3), connection-string NAMES, `access-restriction` list, the active deployment ids (`az webapp log deployment list`) and the build ids (RELAYED from the D53 STATUS if it ended `DEPLOYED:`, else B1286's), the last ARM deployments of the group (`az deployment group list`, names and timestamps only); (3) plan: sku, workers; (4) SQL: server properties (admin type, public network, TLS), database properties (D-4), firewall rules; (5) vault: properties (retention days, purge protection, RBAC) and secret NAMES; (6) role assignments at the group and below (role, principal type, scope; no secrets); (7) activity log of the group since 2026-11-01 (`az monitor activity-log list --start-time 2026-11-01T00:00:00Z`, operation names and times, caller masked); (8) budgets and alert rules, action groups, diagnostic settings that name the demo group (GET only, `az rest --method get` for budgets: `Microsoft.Consumption/budgets` at the group scope); (9) OpenAI account + deployment properties and the storage account properties; (10) a `MANIFEST.tsv` with sha256 of every file. **Property:** the snapshot lets someone rebuild an equivalent demo from `infra/env/demo.bicepparam` plus the notes without reading any hosted secret. Then the secret/host scans of D-9.
**Step 3 - THE GUARDS (D-6), then THE DELETE.** Within 60 seconds: identity pass; `az lock list` x2 = 0; D53 end line re-read; pane list re-read; group resource ids equal to the snapshot's by program (control: one id removed in a scratch copy fails); UAT list sha equal to Step 1's; UAT `/` GET 200; the hard-stop clock. Then, in the same second as an identity pass, `bash delete1303.sh`, which runs exactly `az group delete -n hpsm-poc-demo-rg --yes --no-wait` and logs START (UTC and AEDT). A write that has started is not killed. **There is no way back and no recreate: if the delete is refused, fails or sticks, leave everything as found and end `STOPPED:`.** No second delete command; no member deleted by hand.
**Step 4 - VERIFY (D-2 poll, then).** (a) `az group show` = ResourceGroupNotFound and `az group exists` false (control: the UAT group answers true); the subscription's group names equal the Step 0 list minus the demo group (names only); (b) the two demo hostnames (from the snapshot, held in scratch): DNS and one GET each of `/` with `curl -sS -m 15 --noproxy '*'`: PROPERTY "no longer serves the app": not 2xx, and the demo banner "Review demo: synthetic data only" and the build id x0 (control: the UAT start page is 200 and answers the UAT-only text per Step 0; the check must be able to fail); (c) UAT `/` 200 and UAT resource list sha equal before and after, sites `Running`, `defaultHostName`s equal; (d) the activity-log rows of the delete (`Microsoft.Resources/subscriptions/resourceGroups/delete` Started/Accepted/Succeeded, and member deletes) listed with times, caller masked; (e) the D-8 reads; (f) the budget at the group scope read again (expect not found) and any budget, alert rule or action group still naming the demo group listed; (g) the evidence scans of D-9 over the final folder. Anything that fails with the group already gone is recorded and does not become a second write.
**Step 5 - COST (D-13).** The table: stops billing / retained without charge (the soft-deleted vault until its scheduled purge date, plus whatever D-8 listed) / UNMEASURED. Name anything that still bills (a surviving budget has no charge; an orphan alert rule may).
